course: dictionary
lesson: 14983
title: Filling up again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To replenish something is to fill it up again, or bring it back to the amount it was before. The start of the word, re-, often means again, like in refill.
explain: Use the words around it. «The farmer replenished the water tank before the hot summer.» The tank had been used up, so replenished must mean filled up again. Try the meaning in the sentence: "The farmer filled up the water tank before the hot summer" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: You can also replenish your energy. «After the race, Sam ate a banana to replenish his energy.» Sam was tired, so he ate to feel strong again. It is the same idea: bringing something back to how it was.
explain: Replenish is a formal word, so you will meet it in exams and in science. «Plants replenish oxygen in the air.» Shops replenish stock, and rain replenishes rivers and reservoirs.
fact: Replenish is a verb: replenish, replenishes, replenished, replenishing.
fact: «Replenish» means to fill something up again, or bring it back to the amount it was before.
fact: «Replenish your energy» means to rest, eat or drink so you feel strong again.
fact: Common phrases are «replenish supplies», «replenish stocks» and «replenish your water».
fact: Replenish is a formal word, so it is often used in writing, science and exams.
exercise: «The farmer replenished the water tank.» What does replenished mean? | Left it alone | Painted red | *Filled up again | Emptied out
exercise: «After the race, Sam ate a banana to replenish his energy.» Why did Sam eat the banana? | *To feel strong again | To hide from the crowd | To make the race longer
exercise: «Shops replenish stock.» What do shops do when they replenish stock? | Move to a new street | Sell everything and stop | Close for the day | *Fill their shelves again
test: «Rain replenishes the rivers.» What does replenishes mean here? | Dries them up | *Brings them back to full | Paints them blue | Makes them empty
test: Mia wants to replenish her water bottle. What does she want to do? | Hide it under her bed | Drink it all and stop | Throw the bottle away | *Fill it up again
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to replenish? | Break | Forget | Empty | *Refill
